    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-declaration.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A theme is a palette AND a geometry",
      "prov:value": "**Surfaces must be OPAQUE.** `ThemePaletteSchema.surface` is `z.string()`, so\n`rgba(…, 0.4)` parses — and `themes.test.ts` refuses it anyway, because the\nfloating-sticky rule depends on it (see `theme-artefacts`, and bean `ivfw`).\nA premise a schema cannot hold is a premise that needs a test.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ivfw"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-declaration.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "All three layouts, or the theme is invalid",
      "prov:value": "`laptop`, `mobile`, `card`. The owner: *\"themes need all three layouts to be\ndefined to be considered valid.\"* Not a new vocabulary — exactly the set\n`<name>.json`'s `images[].layout` already uses."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-declaration.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Nothing derives a theme",
      "prov:value": "`ThemedTodoFields.theme` and the landing sticky's required `theme` are the\nwhole selection surface: an id, set by an author. **This is a rule, not a\ngap**, and it has read as a gap to two agents already."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theme-declaration.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the declaration cannot tell you, ever",
      "prov:value": "**Whether the box is on the right thing.** Square, in bounds, and framing a\npatch of sky are compatible — two of the first seven avatar crops were exactly\nthat, and only a render caught them. So:"
    }
  ]
}
